// `volatile` is not a Kama keyword — the MMIO/ISR qualifier is spelled `hardware` (emits C `volatile`).
// The accepted forms are in tests/hardware_static_{flag,ptr}.kama. This guards that `volatile` is never
// silently accepted.
//
// It used to be refused as a plain syntax error. Since §2e.28 it is refused one step earlier, as a
// RESERVED WORD: `volatile` is a C keyword, and kama reserves the whole C set because a kama name that is
// one emits C that does not compile. Either way it is rejected, which is all this fixture claims.
static volatile int32 reg = 0;
fn int32 main() { return 0; }
